content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:38:The SERP is dominated by Perth bariatric clinic cost/fee pages — commercial transactional intent. Top organic results are dedicated /fees, /cost or /program-costs pages from local surgical practices: Obesity Surgery WA (obesitysurgerywa.com.au/fees), Perth Weight Loss Surgery (/cost), Dr Kevin Dolan (gastric-sleeve-costs), Mercy Bariatrics (costs-finance), and Advance Surgical (/pricing). Domain Rating is low across the board (most DR 2–15, highest is Mercy at DR 31), confirming KD 0 and a very winnable SERP. Google surfaces a People Also Ask block (Medicare coverage, disqualifiers, the "30 rule", 10-years-after questions) plus two Reddit threads ranking on financing/super — signalling that informational cost-mechanics and funding questions sit alongside the commercial fee pages. A national informational guide (Healthy Weight Australia "2025 Guide") also ranks, showing room for an educational angle.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:43:| 1 | obesitysurgerywa.com.au | Weight Loss Centre Murdoch & Perth - Fees Obesity Surgery WA |
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:53:3. **Answer the misunderstandings honestly** — the 12-month waiting period as a cost-saving decision, and Medicare NOT covering the hospital admission, are common misunderstandings surfaced in PAA and Reddit but poorly answered by clinic pages; direct, honest coverage wins featured-snippet and AI-citation potential.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:83:Name all the components: surgeon's fee, anaesthetist's fee, assistant surgeon's fee (where applicable), and the hospital fee. Note that there can also be costs for the dietitian, follow-up appointments and pre-operative tests. Each is billed separately — this is why the headline number can feel confusing.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:89:Explain that the biggest determinant of what the patient actually pays is whether they have appropriate private health insurance and whether the waiting period has been served. With the right cover, the hospital fee is largely covered and out-of-pocket drops considerably. Without it, the hospital component becomes a significant self-funded cost.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:92:Short, honest note: every range on this page uses "approximately" or "around" deliberately. Costs move with the procedure, the surgeon's assessment, the insurer's policy and the hospital. The practice does not ask patients to make decisions on a ballpark — a written estimate comes first.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:96:- **Medicare eligibility:** Rebates generally apply where surgery is clinically indicated — typically BMI 35+ or 30+ with an obesity-related health condition. Eligibility is assessed by the surgeon, not assumed.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:97:- **Private health cover — what to check:** Patients generally need gold-tier or equivalent hospital cover that explicitly includes the obesity surgery item numbers. Identify the key Medicare item numbers: 31575 (sleeve) and 31572 (bypass). Stress the difference between a general "weight management" category and the specific item numbers — check the specific items.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:99:- **Medicare and the hospital admission:** Medicare provides a rebate on surgical and consultation fees for eligible patients but does NOT cover the hospital admission for elective bariatric surgery. That cost is either covered by private health or paid out-of-pocket.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:108:3. **Written, itemised estimate** — Before any commitment, a personalised estimate lists the surgeon, anaesthetist, assistant and hospital fees, what the insurer is expected to cover, and the likely out-of-pocket; no surprises is the practice standard
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:127:- Assuming all private health policies cover obesity surgery — many do not; some cover consultations but not the hospital item numbers; always check 31575 and 31572 specifically
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:128:- Overlooking the 12-month waiting period — booking before it is served can mean the entire hospital fee falls on the patient
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:129:- Forgetting that Medicare does not cover the hospital admission — the Medicare rebate applies to surgical and consultation fees, not the hospital stay
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:137:- Without suitable cover: the hospital fee adds significantly to the total
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:138:- Medicare rebates reduce the surgical and consultation portion for eligible patients but do not cover the hospital admission
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:167:3. Does Medicare cover weight loss surgery? (Rebate on surgical and consultation fees for eligible patients; does NOT cover hospital admission; eligibility generally requires BMI 35+ or 30+ with comorbidity)
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:170:6. Why are there several separate fees rather than one price? (Surgeon, anaesthetist, assistant surgeon and hospital each bill independently; dietitian and pre-op tests may also be separate; written estimate lists every component)
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth.md:178:- Medicare's non-coverage of hospital admissions must be stated clearly — a common misunderstanding among patients
