content-reviews/summary.md:25:**3. Medicare/BMI accuracy + cost certainty (must-fix).** Drafts state "BMI 35+, or 30–35 with conditions" next to MBS item numbers; the MBS wording (explanatory note TN.8.29) is BMI 40+, or 35+ with major comorbidities — lower-BMI pathways must read "may be considered for assessment", never "you may qualify". **Brief-inherited:** the sleeve and bypass briefs mandate the 35/30–35 framing — correct the briefs too. Also: item 31581 (BPD/duodenal switch) cited on the Roux-en-Y page (should be 31572 only); single dollar fees quoted against the briefs' no-single-figure rule, plus a literal "$[X,XXX]" placeholder; and absolute insurance claims ("gold-tier… covers/will cover the hospital and theatre component") need policy-, waiting-period- and gap-aware wording.
content-reviews/summary.md:29:**5. Length + FAQ coverage (should-fix).** Body-only counts incl. FAQs (FAQs count toward the target, as agreed 1 Jul): 1,844 / 1,783 / 2,091 / 1,958 / 1,908 vs targets of 1,000–1,500 — roughly 280–900 over. Decide once: enforce the brief targets (per-page cut lists are in the reviews) or consciously accept ~1,800. While cutting, add the missing FAQ topics Google is currently asking (cost *in Perth*, the 30/30 eating rule, who is *not* eligible, Medicare coverage, 10-year outcomes).
content-reviews/summary.md:33:1. **Which hospitals are current?** The briefs say St John of God Murdoch/Subiaco; all five drafts consistently say Mount Private, The Park Private and Waikiki Private, with consults at Garden City Booragoon + WA Cardiology Greenfields (Greenfields = the Mandurah suburb, so that part is just naming granularity). The drafts' consistency suggests the writer has newer information. **Nobody rewrites either direction until this is confirmed** — whichever source is wrong gets corrected.
