content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:394:> **Who is not eligible for gastric bypass?** For Medicare-funded bariatric surgery, a BMI below 40 without a major medical comorbidity, or a BMI below 35, does not meet the stated MBS eligibility threshold. Surgery may also be unsuitable if health risks, anatomy or the ability to follow long-term nutrition and follow-up need further assessment. Eligibility and alternatives must be discussed with your surgeon.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:396:Why it matters: The page should answer the negative eligibility question without implying that a condition, BMI or online checklist guarantees access to surgery.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:410:> The small keyhole incisions mean less pain post-operatively, smaller scars, and generally, a faster recovery than open surgery, though your surgeon will discuss your goals and your different surgical options during your initial consultation.
