content-briefs/book-consultation.md:46:orientation consultation, GP referral, Medicare rebate, private health insurance, no obligation, Booragoon clinic, Mandurah clinic, weight loss surgery options, gastric sleeve, gastric bypass, gastric band, BMI eligibility, recovery and time off work, out-of-pocket cost, bariatric team, first appointment
content-briefs/book-consultation.md:50:The "bariatric surgery perth" SERP is dominated almost entirely by individual Perth bariatric clinic and surgeon homepages (Perth Surgical & Bariatrics, Obesity Surgery WA, Aurora Bariatrics / Dr Ruth Blackham, Perth Weight Loss Surgery / Dr Siva Gounder, Mercy Bariatrics, Advance Surgical, Evolve Bariatrics, Veritas Centre). These are commercial/transactional landing pages, not informational articles. Domain Ratings are low across the board (mostly DR 1–14, with Mercy at 31 and Evolve at 26 the strongest), so the competitive bar is modest. Google injects a People Also Ask block at position 4 with cost, Medicare coverage, disqualification, and "30/30 rule" questions, signalling strong informational sub-intent around cost and Medicare that a booking page should answer via FAQs. No dedicated "consultation booking" page currently ranks — competitors fold booking into generic homepages.
content-briefs/book-consultation.md:64:No competitor ranks a purpose-built "book a consultation" page — they all use generic surgeon/clinic homepages, so there is a clear gap for a dedicated, conversion-focused booking page that owns the "what happens at a consultation / is booking a commitment" intent. The PAA block proves searchers want cost and Medicare answers up front, yet most competing homepages bury or omit pricing; addressing "Medicare rebate via GP referral" and "no minimum BMI to book" directly is a differentiator. Biggest opportunities: (1) explicitly reassure that booking is not committing to surgery and a referral is recommended-but-not-required (no competitor leads with this), (2) Perth-specific dual-location convenience (Booragoon & Mandurah) plus a prominent phone number for high-intent callers, (3) an FAQ section capturing the PAA queries (cost, Medicare, what to bring, pressure on the day). Avoid testimonials/before-after/guaranteed-outcome language per AHPRA/TGA. The exact phrase "bariatric consultation perth" has no measurable Ahrefs volume, so the page should rank by capturing the broader "weight loss surgery perth / gastric sleeve perth / cost" cluster while serving the bottom-funnel booking intent.
content-briefs/book-consultation.md:98:- **Para 2:** Explain what the reader gets from the appointment: time to ask anything, explanation of different procedures, walkthrough of what recovery looks like, open discussion of costs and funding, and a chance to meet the team who would support them — before they make any decision at all.
content-briefs/book-consultation.md:107:- **BMI / eligibility note:** There is no minimum or maximum weight required before booking. A consultation is the right starting point for anyone considering weight loss surgery, even if they are not yet sure it is for them.
content-briefs/book-consultation.md:111:  - Has questions about cost, recovery, time off work, or what life looks like afterwards
content-briefs/hiatus-hernia-repair.md:8:This page serves Australian adults living with reflux, GORD or a diagnosed hiatus hernia who want to understand what surgical repair involves and what it costs. The primary keyword is national in demand, so the page is written primarily as a national resource with a clear Perth section — it explains what a hiatus hernia is, when surgery is indicated, the laparoscopic fundoplication approach, recovery and cost, and positions the practice's upper GI surgeons as the people to assess whether repair is right. It is medically relevant to a bariatric practice because hiatus hernia and reflux commonly accompany or follow weight-loss surgery, especially gastric sleeve.
