content-briefs/hiatus-hernia-repair.md:71:- BMI note: There is no BMI threshold — this is a medically indicated upper GI operation. The decision rests on symptoms, investigations and how well other treatments have worked, not a number.
content-briefs/hiatus-hernia-repair.md:100:- Intro paragraph: Well-established and generally safe, but all surgery carries risk. Note the fundoplication can cause temporary swallowing difficulty or gas-bloat that usually eases; general surgical risks; possible recurrence. Frame as respect for the reader. Most patients do well; surgeon explains how risks apply individually.
