content-briefs/gastric-band.md:98:5. **Hospital Recovery** — Typically one night in hospital; team manages comfort, starts fluids, checks recovery before discharge.
content-briefs/gastric-band.md:107:- Shorter hospital stay and quicker initial recovery than a sleeve or bypass
content-briefs/gastric-band.md:119:  - General surgical risks: bleeding, infection, blood clots, anaesthetic reaction
content-briefs/gastric-band.md:122:Cover: the total cost depends on private health cover, surgeon and anaesthetist fees, hospital stay, and the ongoing adjustment visits the band requires. Note the Medicare item number (31569). Explain that Medicare and most private health funds with appropriate cover contribute toward bariatric surgery, and that some patients use superannuation early release for out-of-pocket costs. Do not quote a single figure. State that every patient receives a clear, itemised written estimate before any decision is made.
