content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:3:**Primary keyword:** bariatric surgery hospital perth
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:8:This page settles the practical question every prospective patient has before booking: where will my surgery actually happen, and where will I be seen before and after? It distinguishes the two surgical hospitals (St John of God Murdoch and Subiaco) from the two consulting locations (Booragoon and Mandurah), and gives accreditation, accessibility and referral context. It builds trust through clarity and accredited-hospital signals, not through promises about outcomes. The reader is deciding whether the locations work for their life before they pick up the phone.
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:17:- Keyword: bariatric surgery hospital perth
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:30:| gastric sleeve hospital perth | 30 | 30 |
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:35:St John of God Murdoch, St John of God Subiaco, accredited private hospital, Garden City Specialist Centre, Booragoon, Marmion Street, WA Cardiology Centre, Mandurah, Minilya Pkwy, consulting rooms, operating theatre, intensive care, recovery ward, laparoscopic, keyhole surgery, FRACS, GP referral, Medicare item number, private health cover, parking, follow-up appointment, day of surgery
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:38:For "bariatric surgery hospital perth" and its variants, the top results split between hospital-system pages (St John of God Health Care's own service pages) and individual bariatric practice "contact" or "locations" pages (the same single-surgeon clinics that dominate the broader Perth bariatric cluster — Dr Kiyingi, Dr Rao, Dr Gounder, Dr Dolan, Aurora, Evolve, Advance Surgical). Most practice pages treat location as an afterthought: a map embed and an address, with little explanation of the difference between where you consult and where you have surgery. Hospital-system pages rank on domain authority but are generic and not practice-specific. Domain ratings across the practice field are low (DR 2–26), so the cluster is winnable on relevance and clear on-page logistics rather than backlinks. Expect a People Also Ask block covering "where is bariatric surgery done in Perth", "is bariatric surgery covered by Medicare", and hospital-name queries — these should be answered directly in FAQ schema.
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:50:Opportunity 1: No ranking competitor clearly separates the two kinds of location — where you consult versus where you have surgery. Most patients are confused about whether the hospital and the rooms are the same place; a page that explains this plainly fills a real gap and earns the PAA real estate. Opportunity 2: The Mandurah consulting option is a genuine differentiator for patients south of Perth who otherwise assume they must travel into the city for every visit — few competitors surface a southern consulting location. Opportunity 3: Competitors rarely explain *why* an accredited private hospital with theatre and ICU backup matters; framing accreditation as a safety signal (not a boast) is useful consumer guidance the field ignores. Opportunity 4: Practical logistics — parking, one phone number across locations, referral before booking — are demanded by searchers but thinly covered. Note: low overall DR across the SERP means strong on-page specificity (named hospitals, named consulting addresses, accreditation, one contact number) plus FAQ schema is likely enough to break into the top half.
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:61:- **Subheadline:** Warm, direct, practical. Acknowledge that settling where surgery will happen and where they will be seen is a reasonable early concern. Name the two accredited private hospitals (St John of God Murdoch and Subiaco) and the two consulting locations (Booragoon and Mandurah). One to two sentences.
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:65:1. **Surgical hospitals / 2** — St John of God Murdoch and St John of God Subiaco
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:67:3. **Hospital type / Private** — accredited private hospitals
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:70:### Where Obesity Surgery WA operates and consults (3 paragraphs)
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:72:**Paragraph 1 — The surgical hospitals**
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:73:Describe St John of God Murdoch and St John of God Subiaco as accredited private hospitals in Perth with full theatres, recovery wards and intensive-care backup on site. Explain that which hospital is used depends on the surgeon's operating lists and the patient's circumstances, confirmed well before the day. Factual and grounded.
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:76:Explain that most appointments happen in the consulting rooms, not at the hospital. Name Booragoon (Garden City Specialist Centre, 537 Marmion Street) as the main Perth rooms and Mandurah (WA Cardiology Centre, 30 Minilya Pkwy) as the southern option so patients do not have to travel into Perth for every visit.
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:79:Clarify the distinction: consulting rooms are where you meet your surgeon, have assessment and return for follow-up; the hospitals are where the operation and in-hospital recovery happen. Note one phone number, (08) 9332 0066, covers all locations.
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:82:A short, practical paragraph for readers weighing where to have surgery. Tell them what actually matters: an accredited private hospital, a full operating theatre and intensive-care backup on the same site, and ease of getting to follow-up appointments. Genuine consumer guidance, not a competitive put-down.
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:85:Frame as "what to know before your visit", not BMI eligibility (omit the BMI callout for this page). Cover:
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:87:- Consultations are in Booragoon and Mandurah, not at the hospital
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:88:- Surgery and in-hospital recovery are at St John of God Murdoch or Subiaco (accredited private hospitals)
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:89:- Both hospitals are private, so appropriate private hospital cover (or self-funding) is relevant; the team explains options before booking
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:99:5. **Hospital Recovery** — Recovery in hospital (usually a few nights) with nursing and dietitian support before discharge
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:104:- Surgery at accredited private hospitals (Murdoch and Subiaco) with full theatre, recovery and ICU backup on site
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:115:**Opening paragraph:** State that choosing an accredited private hospital with theatre and ICU backup is part of having surgery done safely, but that no hospital or surgeon can remove the risks surgery carries. The location gives the safest possible setting; it does not change the honest fact that any operation has risks.
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:124:Explain that because surgery is at private hospitals, costs depend on the procedure, private health cover level and individual circumstances. Note that most bariatric procedures attract a Medicare item number and that patients with appropriate private hospital cover typically pay a gap, not the full fee. Mention early superannuation access as an option some use. Emphasise a written estimate is provided before any commitment. Do not quote dollar figures on this page.
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:144:1. Where is the surgery actually performed? (St John of God Murdoch or Subiaco; accredited private hospitals; confirmed before the day)
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:145:2. Where are consultations held? (Booragoon — Garden City Specialist Centre, 537 Marmion Street; and Mandurah — WA Cardiology Centre, 30 Minilya Pkwy; not at the hospital)
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:147:4. What is the difference between the consulting rooms and the hospital? (Rooms = meet surgeon, assessment, follow-up; hospital = operation and recovery)
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:148:5. Which hospital will my surgery be at, Murdoch or Subiaco? (Depends on operating lists and circumstances; both accredited private hospitals; confirmed beforehand)
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:149:6. Is parking available at the consulting rooms and hospitals? (On-site patient parking at both hospital campuses and the specialist centres; mention access needs when booking)
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:150:7. Are these public or private hospitals? (Both private and accredited; private cover or self-funding relevant; most procedures attract a Medicare item number)
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:157:- Use only the confirmed hard facts: hospitals (SJOG Murdoch and Subiaco), consulting addresses (Booragoon — Garden City Specialist Centre, 537 Marmion Street; Mandurah — WA Cardiology Centre, 30 Minilya Pkwy), phone (08) 9332 0066. Do not invent additional addresses, suite numbers, opening hours or specifics.
content-briefs/hospitals-locations.md:161:- No "the best", "Perth's leading", "world-class", or superiority claims about the hospitals or the practice — accreditation may be stated factually because it is verifiable.
