docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/am-i-eligible-codex.md:161:Why it matters: the brief explicitly asks for a "general information, not medical advice - individual assessment required" line. This is especially important because the page discusses BMI thresholds.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/am-i-eligible-codex.md:187:> A surgical eligibility assessment gives you a personalised answer based on BMI, weight-related health conditions, previous weight loss attempts, medical risk, readiness for aftercare, and your goals.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/am-i-eligible-codex.md:212:The core medical structure is strong, but revise BMI/mental-health/safety claims into "assessment criteria" language and add a direct "who is not eligible" answer.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/SUMMARY.md:4:**How to read this pack:** start here, then open the per-page file for whichever page you're working on — `gastric-sleeve-perth.md`, `gastric-bypass-perth.md`, `bariatric-surgery-perth.md`, `weight-loss-surgery-perth.md`, `am-i-eligible.md`. Every issue in those files comes with the exact draft quote and a paste-ready rewrite. Fresh keyword/SERP data is in `../ahrefs-refresh-2026-07-10.md`. (`_worklog/` is internal working notes — ignore.)
