docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:107:   > BMI 35–40 and a related condition such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, sleep apnoea, joint disease, or gastro-oesophageal reflux disease (GORD): surgery is commonly considered
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:109:   > BMI 30–35: may be considered in select cases, often where diabetes is difficult to manage with medication alone; assessed on an individual basis
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:111:   > Eligibility is assessed individually. For a Medicare-listed bariatric surgery pathway, the relevant MBS thresholds are BMI 40+ or BMI 35+ with a major co-morbidity; a BMI below 35 does not meet that MBS threshold. Your surgeon must assess the clinical options, risks and suitability for your circumstances.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:113:   This replaces the implication that BMI 30-35 is a surgical pathway and avoids treating “may be considered” as eligibility.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:120:   > Costs depend on the pathway, procedure, hospital, private health cover, waiting periods, hospital excess, anaesthetist and other fees. Any applicable estimate or range should be discussed at consultation after your team understands your situation; no fixed cost applies to everyone. Confirm any Medicare rebate or private-cover contribution for your circumstances.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:122:   > **9. What is the 30/30 eating rule after surgery?**
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:123:   > A commonly used 30/30 approach is to avoid drinking for about 30 minutes before a meal and wait about 30 minutes after eating before drinking again. Your dietitian or surgeon will confirm whether this applies at your stage of recovery and give you the relevant eating and drinking plan.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:126:   > The MBS thresholds are BMI 40+ or BMI 35+ with a major co-morbidity. A person below BMI 35 does not meet that MBS threshold; a person at BMI 35-39.9 needs the relevant major co-morbidity. Clinical suitability also depends on medical history, surgical risk, readiness for follow-up and individual clinician assessment.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:129:   > Medicare may provide rebates for eligible specialist consultations and MBS-listed bariatric surgery services when current criteria are met. The relevant procedure items are 31575 for sleeve gastrectomy, 31572 for Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and 31581 for BPD/duodenal switch. Private health cover, waiting periods, hospital excess and anaesthetist fees can affect out-of-pocket costs, so confirm what applies before deciding.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:134:   Verify the clinic's exact 30/30 protocol and the current MBS wording before publication. These answers contain no dollar figures; any cost range belongs in the consultation discussion.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:154:> If you are researching weight loss surgery Perth options, Obesity Surgery WA can help you compare surgical, medical and dietitian-led pathways without pressure.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:168:> Obesity Surgery WA is a specialist team of surgeons, physicians, dietitians, and exercise physiologists who have been supporting weight loss in Perth for over 20 years.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:170:> Obesity Surgery WA brings together surgeons, physicians, Accredited Practising Dietitians and exercise physiologists, with 20+ years supporting weight loss in Perth, clinics in Booragoon and Mandurah, and individual medical assessment available for some people at BMI 27+ where clinically appropriate.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:176:> You may be eligible for weight loss surgery if you have a BMI of 40 or higher, or 35 or higher with a weight-related health condition such as type 2 diabetes or high blood pressure, and where diet and exercise alone have not produced long-term results.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:178:> A BMI of 27 or above, particularly where a weight-related health condition is present, is a reason to request an individual medical assessment for non-surgical options. Surgical Medicare eligibility must be assessed separately; current MBS criteria refer to BMI 40+ or BMI 35+ with a major co-morbidity, with suitability assessed by your surgeon.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:186:> Is weight loss surgery covered by Medicare in Australia? Medicare may provide rebates for eligible specialist consultations and MBS-listed bariatric surgery services when current criteria are met. The relevant procedure items are 31575 for sleeve gastrectomy, 31572 for Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and 31581 for BPD/duodenal switch. Private health cover, waiting periods, hospital excess and anaesthetist fees can affect out-of-pocket costs, so confirm what applies before deciding.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:194:> The cost of weight loss treatment in Perth depends on the pathway: medical management, dietitian-led programs and surgery all have different fee structures, and surgical costs also vary by procedure, private health cover, hospital excess and anaesthetist fees. Some patients explore approved payment or funding pathways, but these should be discussed separately and should not influence whether treatment is clinically appropriate.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:241:> We have consulting rooms in Booragoon and Greenfields, keeping appointments accessible for patients across Perth and the south-west. Surgeries are performed at [<u>Mount Private Hospital</u>](https://mountprivatehospital.com.au), [<u>The Park Private Hospital</u>](https://www.tpph.com.au/), and [<u>Waikiki Private Hospital</u>](https://waikikiprivate.com.au/). Once your surgery is planned, our team will walk you through exactly what to expect, where to go, and who will be involved at every stage, so there are no surprises on the day.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:243:> We have consulting rooms in Booragoon and Mandurah, keeping appointments accessible for patients across Perth and the south-west. Surgeries are performed at [hospital identity to be verified]. Once your surgery is planned, our team will walk you through exactly what to expect, where to go, and who will be involved at every stage.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:251:> Surgery is not the only pathway forward. Because obesity is a medical condition — not a willpower failure — the right treatment looks different for every person. Options range from [non-surgical weight loss](/osw/content/non-surgical-weight-loss), [weight-loss medication](/osw/content/weight-loss-medication) and [dietitian-led support](/osw/content/bariatric-dietitian-perth) through to [bariatric surgery](/osw/content/bariatric-surgery-perth), including [gastric sleeve](/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-perth), [gastric bypass](/osw/content/gastric-bypass-perth) and [gastric band](/osw/content/gastric-band).
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:292:Summary: Main fixes are to separate surgical eligibility from medical management, add direct Medicare/minimum-BMI/cost FAQs, and cut 500+ words.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:297:- **Hospitals:** Use the canonical paste-ready surgery-location replacement in Should fix 8b above. The hospital identity remains unverified until the client confirms the correct facilities; do not choose one side in the copy.
src/app/osw/content/weight-loss-surgery-perth/page.tsx:5:  title: "Weight Loss Surgery Perth | Obesity Surgery WA Perth",
src/app/osw/content/weight-loss-surgery-perth/page.tsx:6:  description: "Weight loss surgery in Perth at Obesity Surgery WA. Gastric sleeve, bypass, banding and medical management. Understand your eligibility, costs and what to expect from our specialist bariatric team.",
src/app/osw/content/weight-loss-surgery-perth/page.tsx:16:    "Weight loss surgery in Perth at Obesity Surgery WA. Gastric sleeve, bypass, banding and medical management. Understand your eligibility, costs and what to expect from our specialist bariatric team.",
src/app/osw/content/weight-loss-surgery-perth/page.tsx:20:    "If you have spent years trying to lose weight and keep it off, you are not the problem, and you are not alone. Obesity Surgery WA is a Perth team of surgeons, physicians and dietitians who help you find the right pathway, whether that starts with medical management or with surgery. We meet you where you are.",
src/app/osw/content/weight-loss-surgery-perth/page.tsx:26:    { label: "Starting BMI", value: "27+", note: "May be suitable for the medical team" },
src/app/osw/content/weight-loss-surgery-perth/page.tsx:33:    "This is why Obesity Surgery WA is not just a group of surgeons. Our team includes physicians who manage the medical side of weight, and specialist dietitians whose support is a key part of why people succeed long term. Whoever you see first, you are stepping into a team that can move you along the spectrum of care as your needs change.",
src/app/osw/content/weight-loss-surgery-perth/page.tsx:40:    "You do not need a very high BMI to start a conversation. A BMI of 27 or above, particularly with a weight-related health condition, may make you suitable to see our medical team. Higher BMI ranges are typically where surgical options are discussed. We will help you work out where you sit.",
src/app/osw/content/weight-loss-surgery-perth/page.tsx:42:    "If your BMI is around 27 or higher and you have a condition such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure or sleep apnoea, our medical team can review non-surgical options with you.",
src/app/osw/content/weight-loss-surgery-perth/page.tsx:43:    "If your BMI is higher and previous attempts at weight loss have not held, surgery may be worth discussing alongside medical management.",
src/app/osw/content/weight-loss-surgery-perth/page.tsx:89:    "Every option on the spectrum carries its own considerations, and we will not pretend otherwise. Medications can have side effects and may not suit everyone. Very low calorie diets need medical supervision. Surgery is a significant step with real risks and a recovery period. Choosing the right pathway means weighing these against the risks of leaving obesity untreated, which are also serious. Your clinician will go through your individual situation in detail before you commit to anything.",
src/app/osw/content/weight-loss-surgery-perth/page.tsx:124:        "Yes, and many people do exactly that. A large part of what we do is help people who are unsure where to start. If your BMI is around 27 or above, our medical team can talk through non-surgical options such as medication and dietitian-supported plans. You are not committing to surgery by booking a consultation. You are simply finding out what your options are.",
src/app/osw/wireframes/page.tsx:5:  description: "Page templates, homepage wireframe, and contact/booking flow UX for the Obesity Surgery WA rebuild.",
src/app/osw/wireframes/page.tsx:66:                note: "H1: [Procedure] Perth. 1–2 sentence patient benefit. 3 CTAs: Am I eligible? / What will it cost? / Book consultation. Trust bar: surgeon count, hospital logos, years.",
src/app/osw/wireframes/page.tsx:71:                note: "4 cards: Expected excess weight loss %, procedure time, hospital stay, recovery time. Scannable. Evidence-linked.",
src/app/osw/wireframes/page.tsx:81:                note: "BMI tiers (27+, 30+, 35+). Comorbidity triggers. CTA → /am-i-eligible.",
src/app/osw/wireframes/page.tsx:156:              note="H1: Perth's Bariatric Surgery Specialists. Subhead: [Surgeons, hospital affiliations, years]. CTAs: Am I eligible? / What will it cost? / Book a consultation. Trust badges: RACS fellow, St John of God, X procedures."
src/app/osw/wireframes/page.tsx:170:            <WireBlock label="FAQ ACCORDION (8–10)" note="Cost, eligibility, Medicare, recovery, team, location. FAQ schema on all answers." />
src/app/osw/wireframes/page.tsx:171:            <WireBlock label="LOCATION MAP + DETAILS" note="Booragoon / Murdoch / Subiaco / Mandurah. Address + phone + hospital affiliations." />
src/app/osw/wireframes/page.tsx:173:            <WireBlock label="FOOTER" note="Full nav | RACS / hospital accreditations | Phone | Legal disclaimer | AHPRA registration numbers" />
