docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:7:- MBS Online item 31572 is Roux-en-Y gastric bypass; item 31575 is sleeve gastrectomy; item 31581 is biliopancreatic diversion with or without duodenal switch. MBS explanatory note TN.8.29 says clinically severe obesity generally means BMI 40+, or BMI 35+ with major medical co-morbidities, with population variation and final clinical judgment by the surgeon. Sources: https://www9.health.gov.au/mbs/fullDisplay.cfm?q=31572&type=item, https://www9.health.gov.au/mbs/fullDisplay.cfm?q=31575&type=item, https://www9.health.gov.au/mbs/fullDisplay.cfm?q=31581&type=item.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:10:- PrivateHealth.gov.au confirms weight loss surgery is a Gold-tier hospital category, but coverage and out-of-pocket exposure still depend on the policy, waiting periods, hospital agreements, excesses/co-payments, and gap arrangements. Sources: https://www.privatehealth.gov.au/health_insurance/howitworks/producttiers.htm, https://www.privatehealth.gov.au/health_insurance/howitworks/waiting_periods.htm, https://www.privatehealth.gov.au/health_insurance/howitworks/out_of_pocket.htm.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:20:   Why: the package itself correctly says the embedded brief above the title is not publishable body. Per the task note, "the publishable body starts at the page title." The real blocking hygiene issues are the in-body scaffolding, such as `extracted/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:81`: "Closing comparison note:", `extracted/gastric-bypass-perth.md:240`: "Conversion CTA headline:", and `extracted/am-i-eligible.md:157`: "Option A / Am I Eligible for Weight Loss Surgery?" So this summary finding should be narrowed, not kept as written.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:22:2. `review/gastric-sleeve-perth-codex.md` overstates the hospital-name issue by calling the draft facilities wrong.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:24:   Review quote: `review/gastric-sleeve-perth-codex.md:23-27`: "The brief says SJOG Murdoch/Subiaco and the live OSW consistency work also points there; the draft substitutes unrelated hospital names. Wrong facility names are a factual and E-E-A-T problem. Rewrite to the verified current hospital footprint before publication."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:30:   Why: the summary frames this fairly as a source-of-truth question; the sleeve review treats it as already disproven. The finding should say "verify current hospital footprint before publication" rather than instructing the writer to rewrite to SJOG Murdoch/Subiaco until the client confirms.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:34:   Review quote: `review/bariatric-surgery-perth-codex.md:31-35`: "Medicare and private-health coverage must not be framed as broadly applying to 'most' procedures or as blanket hospital/theatre coverage. The brief requires MBS item-specific, eligibility-dependent wording and warns against overpromising cost outcomes."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:36:   Draft quote: `extracted/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:248-255`: "The good news is that a significant portion is usually covered if you have private health insurance. Medicare rebates apply to most bariatric procedures when eligibility criteria are met... Private health insurance generally covers hospital, theatre and accommodation costs for eligible patients."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:38:   Official-source check: MBS Online confirms there are bariatric item numbers and the BMI framing in TN.8.29 is real; PrivateHealth.gov.au confirms weight loss surgery is a Gold hospital category, but benefits are still policy- and gap-dependent.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:40:   Why: the finding should not imply MBS item references or the broad BMI framework are suspect. The blocker is the draft's certainty and breadth: "most bariatric procedures," "significant portion is usually covered," and hospital/theatre coverage need item-specific, policy-specific, gap-aware wording.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:72:   Draft quote: `extracted/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:233-237`: "Medicare item number 31575 does attract a rebate when eligibility criteria are met, and private health insurance (typically a gold-tier or equivalent policy) covers the hospital and theatre component."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:74:   Draft quote: `extracted/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:307-315`: "Private health insurance with a gold-tier (or equivalent) policy will cover the hospital component."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:78:   Why: official private-health guidance supports Gold-tier category relevance, not a guaranteed hospital/theatre coverage outcome. This is the same class of cost-certainty problem already blocked in `review/gastric-bypass-perth-codex.md:5-7` and `review/bariatric-surgery-perth-codex.md:29-35`.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:84:   Definitive version: `review/gastric-sleeve-perth-codex.md:25-27`: "Wrong facility names are a factual and E-E-A-T problem. Rewrite to the verified current hospital footprint before publication."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:96:   Resolution: distinguish extraction artifacts above the title from true in-body scaffolding. The writer should fix actual body artifacts like `extracted/gastric-bypass-perth.md:240`: "Conversion CTA headline:" and `extracted/am-i-eligible.md:157`: "Option A / Am I Eligible for Weight Loss Surgery?"
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:100:   Blocked on bariatric hub: `review/bariatric-surgery-perth-codex.md:31-35`: "Medicare and private-health coverage must not be framed as broadly applying to 'most' procedures or as blanket hospital/theatre coverage."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:102:   Left uncaught on sleeve: `extracted/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:233-237`: "private health insurance (typically a gold-tier or equivalent policy) covers the hospital and theatre component" and `extracted/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:313-315`: "Private health insurance with a gold-tier (or equivalent) policy will cover the hospital component."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:112:   Per-page evidence: `review/gastric-bypass-perth-codex.md:35-117` contains 21 `- Finding:` entries in the Should-fix section.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:136:   Counter-evidence: `review/cross-page-findings.md:8`: "gastric-bypass-perth: 1,783 body words; target 1,300-1,500; over max by ~283 words."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:142:   Summary quote: `review/SUMMARY.md:20`: "Medicare/BMI guidance needs tightening. The reviews correctly distinguish MBS eligibility framing (BMI 40+, or 35+ with major comorbidities) from the drafts' broader procedure-suitability thresholds, and they correctly flag item 31581 as BPD/duodenal-switch rather than Roux-en-Y bypass."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:144:   Verification: MBS Online confirms item 31572 is Roux-en-Y gastric bypass, 31575 is sleeve gastrectomy, 31581 is biliopancreatic diversion with or without duodenal switch, and TN.8.29 contains the BMI 40+ / 35+ with major co-morbidities framing.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:148:6. Leave the hospital-names question in the summary, but align per-page reviews to it.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:152:   Draft evidence: `extracted/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:149-152`, `extracted/gastric-bypass-perth.md:321-328`, `extracted/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:323-331`, `extracted/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:264-275`, and `extracted/am-i-eligible.md:149-153` all use the Mount Private / The Park / Waikiki footprint.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/final-pass-codex-xhigh.md:158:The package is not ready to send as-is. Most existing REWORK verdicts are directionally right, and the MBS item/BMI characterisation is accurate, but the package needs edits for two overstatements, one misclassified extraction artifact, four missed blockers, and count/theme corrections in the summary.
