src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:24:    { label: "Private cover", value: "Required", note: "Appropriate hospital cover tier needed" },
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:29:    "There is no single price tag for gastric sleeve surgery. The total cost is made up of several separate fees that are billed by different providers. Each of these can vary depending on your situation, your hospital cover and your individual health needs.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:30:    "The main components are the surgeon's fee, the anaesthetist's fee, the hospital (facility) fee, and physician or dietitian fees for assessment and follow-up. Because each is billed separately, two patients can pay different amounts even for the same operation. This is normal in private surgery across Australia.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:36:    "Gastric sleeve surgery is generally suitable for patients with a BMI of 35+, or BMI 30+ with related health conditions such as type 2 diabetes, sleep apnoea or high blood pressure.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:38:    "Medicare rebates and a recognised surgical item number generally apply only when you meet defined clinical eligibility, which usually includes a BMI threshold.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:39:    "Private health funds require an appropriate level of hospital cover that includes bariatric (weight loss) surgery, often a higher tier, and many apply a 12-month waiting period.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:52:        "You meet the team, discuss whether a sleeve is right for you, and receive a written, itemised cost estimate covering surgeon, anaesthetist and hospital fees.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:67:        "Most patients stay around two nights. The hospital facility fee covers your room, theatre and nursing care during this admission.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:78:    "Keyhole (laparoscopic) surgery at accredited private hospitals, St John of God Murdoch and Subiaco.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:85:    "The biggest financial risk is an unexpected out-of-pocket gap. This usually happens when patients do not check their private health cover, are unaware of waiting periods, or compare only the surgeon's fee while forgetting the hospital and anaesthetist. Knowing every fee in advance is the best way to avoid stress later.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:88:    "Inadequate or recently upgraded hospital cover can mean a waiting period or limited benefit.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:93:    "For patients with appropriate private hospital cover, out-of-pocket costs after Medicare and fund rebates typically range from $2,000 to $8,000, depending on your specific policy, excess and surgeon fees. For patients who are self-funded or have inadequate cover, the total cost is typically $15,000 to $30,000 or more. We provide a written itemised estimate specific to your situation before you make any decisions. Patients without suitable cover, or who are within a waiting period, may be eligible to apply to access part of their superannuation on compassionate or medical grounds, and some choose third-party payment plans. During your orientation consultation we walk through each fee line by line so you know exactly where you stand.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:113:        "The total cost of a gastric sleeve in Perth depends on whether you have appropriate private hospital cover. For privately insured patients with a gold-tier or equivalent policy that includes bariatric surgery, out-of-pocket costs after Medicare and fund rebates typically range from $2,000 to $8,000. For self-funded patients without adequate cover, the total cost is typically $15,000 to $30,000 or more. We provide a written itemised estimate for your specific situation at no obligation. MBS item 31575 applies to the surgical component.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:118:        "In private surgery, different providers bill independently. Your surgeon, your anaesthetist and the hospital each charge for their part of your care, and physicians or dietitians may bill for assessment and follow-up. We bring these together in one estimate so nothing is hidden.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:128:        "You generally need hospital cover that includes bariatric or weight loss surgery, which is often a higher policy tier, and many funds apply a 12-month waiting period. We help you check your policy and confirm what your fund will contribute before you commit.",
src/app/osw/content/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth/page.tsx:148:        "Some patients do experience loose skin after significant weight loss, which varies between individuals and is something to discuss with your surgeon. After a recovery and reintroduction period guided by your dietitian, most people eat a wide range of healthy foods, just in smaller portions.",
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-sleeve-perth-codex.md:13:### 2. MBS/BMI eligibility is not accurate enough for Medicare item 31575
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-sleeve-perth-codex.md:15:Quoted draft sentence: "A sleeve gastrectomy is generally considered suitable for adults with a BMI of 35 or higher, or a BMI of 30–35 with associated weight-related health conditions such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, sleep apnoea, or reflux."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-sleeve-perth-codex.md:17:Suggested rewrite: "For Medicare item 31575, clinically severe obesity is generally described as a BMI of 40 or higher, or a BMI of 35 or higher with major medical co-morbidities such as diabetes or cardiovascular disease; suitability for surgery is still assessed individually by the surgeon, and BMI thresholds may vary for some population groups."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-sleeve-perth-codex.md:19:Why this blocks: the draft's BMI 30-35 framing may be a broader clinical eligibility statement, but it should not sit unqualified on a page that also discusses Medicare item 31575.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-sleeve-perth-codex.md:21:### 3. The hospital locations conflict with the brief and undermine trust
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-sleeve-perth-codex.md:23:Quoted draft sentence: "You’ll spend 1-2 nights recuperating at [<u>Mount Private Hospital</u>](https://mountprivatehospital.com.au), [<u>The Park Private Hospital</u>](https://www.tpph.com.au/), or [<u>Waikiki Private Hospital</u>](https://waikikiprivate.com.au/) in Perth."
