content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-92-### Eligibility
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md:93:- **BMI note:** Eligibility is assessed individually. For Medicare-funded bariatric surgery, MBS criteria generally describe clinically severe obesity as a BMI of 40 or higher, or a BMI of 35 or higher with a major medical comorbidity. A BMI below those thresholds does not meet these MBS criteria; any other clinical discussion must be confirmed by the surgical team.
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-94-- **Bullet points to address:**
--
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-107-3. **Pre-operative assessment** — The patient sees dietitians and physicians to prepare for surgery and plan nutrition. Some patients follow a short pre-surgery eating plan to reduce liver size as directed by the team. This is team-led support, not a handout.
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md:108:4. **Surgery** — Keyhole procedure, approximately two hours under general anaesthetic, at St John of God Murdoch or Subiaco. Keep language clinical and calm.
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-109-5. **Hospital recovery** — Typically 2–3 nights. The care team manages comfort, starts the patient on fluids, and monitors movement and recovery, reflecting the complexity of the operation.
--
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-116-
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md:117:1. Clinical averages around 70–80% of excess weight, though individual results vary and no outcome is guaranteed.
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-118-2. Type 2 diabetes may improve for some patients — some may reduce or stop medication after discussion with their doctor; outcomes vary between individuals.
--
